gh to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 67% in the 2020 crash and 38% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades only 5% below its DCF fair value of $81.10, a thin margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 10%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $62.11 to $108 (P10-P90).","Multiples send mixed signals against Consumer Cyclical peers: cheaper on EV/EBITDA 8.4 vs 11.2 and P/FCF 9.7 vs 16.5, richer on P/E 27.2 vs 19.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 32% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 10.3% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $98.20 on average, 27% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 30% clears the cost of capital of 8.8% by 21pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.33).","It converts 14% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 2.00x, but high accruals (-8.8% of assets).","ROE of 40% is amplified by 4.6x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 1.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.7x net debt to EBITDA ($108.4M of cash against $1.1B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 5.4x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.2% over 3 years and 8.5% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 13%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 14.2% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 11%.","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (0.7% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.1%, and 